  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 125 PM EDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nHigh pressure dominates tonight into Monday with tranquil weather \nand a beautiful day expected for the Mackinac Bridge Walk. Only \nweather feature will be a few areas of fog tonight, quickly \ndissipating after sunrise.  \n\nSfc high pressure begins to slide east later Monday, as ridging \naloft slides overhead by early Tuesday consequent of approaching \nPacNW energy ejecting into the Plains. Initial batch of warm and \nmoisture advection expected on Tuesday, focusing across the E UP and \nadjacent areas, spreading south with time later Tuesday and Tuesday \nnight. Moisture is expected to be quite anomalous, and so a wetting \nrain is possible given the atmospheric variables and mechanisms \nremain as progged. Unclear how convective some of this activity will \nbe or how much of the instability will be utilized, which will \ndirectly correlate with rain rates. Nevertheless, current forecast \nhas modest to healthy rains overspreading the region Tuesday night. \nShower chances remain into the early portions of Wednesday most \nlikely, although appears low level moisture hangs around through \nmuch of the day with dewpoints in the 60s, with increasingly windy \nconditions.\n\nIn addition to the precipitation chances, combination of sfc high \npressure sliding off to the east and approaching low pressure mid \nweek will result in a tightening pressure gradient and increasing \nwinds aloft. Consequently, sfc winds will increase, with breezy \nsouthwest to west winds on Wednesday. Current progged soundings from \nGFS bufkit show ~20-30KTs of momentum transfer, resulting in 25 to \n35 mph wind gusts on Wednesday. \n\nCool advection behind this system will knock down temperatures \nacross the region some 10 degrees or so, although not too far off \nfrom climo norms. Temps will be in the mid to upper 60s across the E \nUP and interior northern lower with low 70s in spots. Breezy \nconditions are expected as well. Friday will be beautiful with temps \nin the 70s and plenty of sun.\n\nInteresting pattern upcoming in the extended this weekend and \nbeyond. Models hinting at several areas of troughing, one to the \nnorth across Canada and one potentially digging somewhere across the \nPlains. Both ECMWF and GFS suggest corridor of moisture advects \nnorthward with the potential for rounds of rain. Uncertainty is \nquite high though, with some low probs (10-20%) for 0.5\" of rain \nthrough the weekend and NBM precip probs at 30-40%. Meanwhile, \ndeterministic guidance is quite bullish across northern Michigan and \nthe adjacent Upper Midwest in regards to rain/storms. We'll have to \nsee how all these pieces play together in the coming days.",
